1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:00,940
Hello pool owners.

2
00:00:01,159 --> 00:00:07,639
If your pool looks like this, chances are you want your pool looking like this.

3
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:15,179
In this video, we're going to walk you through the steps of turning your green swampy pool into a crystal clear oasis.

4
00:00:16,239 --> 00:00:18,039
The number one cause of a green pool is algae.

5
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:22,239
Algae will start to grow in your swimming pool if there's a lack of sanitizing agents in the water.

6
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:26,579
Chlorine is by far the most popular and most effective sanitizer that's being used in swimming pools today.

7
00:00:27,359 --> 00:00:30,739
If you have a green pool, you must likely have little or no chlorine in your water.

8
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,579
Maintaining a proper chlorine level is the key to unlocking a crystal clear pool.

9
00:00:35,539 --> 00:00:39,920
Here at Inyo Pools, we have adopted the SLAM method for cleaning your green pool.

10
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:44,159
The SLAM method was coined by our friends over at TroubleFreePool.com

11
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:46,619
and stands for Shock Level and Maintain.

12
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:53,460
This means you will bring your chlorine up to shock level and maintain the pool at shock level until the algae is killed off.

13
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:58,840
In this video, we will show the SLAM method being used to clear up a pool that we worked on in Longwood, Florida.

14
00:00:59,479 --> 00:01:02,659
This pool had been neglected for four years and it literally turned into a swamp.

15
00:01:02,939 --> 00:01:07,219
We're talking about hundreds of tadpoles, frogs, and four years worth of sludge, dirt, and debris.

16
00:01:08,079 --> 00:01:10,159
Even though this was an extreme case of a green pool syndrome,

17
00:01:10,359 --> 00:01:12,879
the same method can be applied to any green pool scenario.

18
00:01:13,939 --> 00:01:16,120
Before starting, you're going to need some essential items.

19
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:21,459
First, an FAS DVD test kit is required to measure free chlorine at high levels.

20
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:25,799
We recommend the TF100 kit from tftestkits.net.

21
00:01:26,079 --> 00:01:30,920
Next, you'll need also a telescopic pool, net, brush, and vacuum.

22
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:34,120
The first step would be to clear your pool of debris.

23
00:01:34,739 --> 00:01:37,959
Organic material is a consumer of chlorine and the more you can remove early on,

24
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:39,540
the less chlorine you'll need to use later.

25
00:01:40,219 --> 00:01:44,120
Depending on how bad your pool is, the debris removal can be a big project or small.

26
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:46,280
In the case of the pool we were working on,

27
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:50,879
this was one of the more time-consuming parts of the process as there was an extreme amount of debris in the pool.

28
00:01:52,159 --> 00:01:55,620
Surface skim, deep net, and vacuum as much debris as possible.

29
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:59,079
If your pool floor is extremely dirty, as in our case,

30
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:02,280
we recommend vacuuming to waste to avoid clogging up your filter.

31
00:02:03,620 --> 00:02:05,659
The next step is to test and treat your pool water.

32
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:10,199
It's best to start out by testing your pH because once you start to slam the pool with chlorine,

33
00:02:10,719 --> 00:02:12,180
your pH readings will not be accurate.

34
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:15,280
Your pH should be between 7.5 and 7.8.

35
00:02:15,819 --> 00:02:20,240
If your pH is above 7.8, use muriatic acid or pH decreaser to lower the level.

36
00:02:21,159 --> 00:02:25,560
If your pH is below 7.5, use pH increaser or soda ash to raise the level.

37
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:31,919
Next, you'll need to test the cyanuric acid in your pool, also known as CYA or stabilizer.

38
00:02:32,099 --> 00:02:37,259
The relationship between free chlorine and CYA is possibly the cornerstone of the slam process.

39
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:43,979
As mentioned before, chlorine is consumed by organic material, but is also consumed by UV rays from the sun.

40
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:47,759
CYA acts as sunscreen for your chlorine.

41
00:02:47,939 --> 00:02:51,879
If it is too low, the chlorine will rapidly be consumed by the hot summer sun.

42
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:57,060
However, if your CYA is too high, the chlorine's effectiveness will greatly be reduced.

43
00:02:57,340 --> 00:03:01,900
30 to 60 parts per million CYA is an ideal range for non-saltwater pools.

44
00:03:02,099 --> 00:03:05,539
For saltwater pools, 70 to 80 parts per million is recommended.

45
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:09,379
If your CYA is above or below the recommended levels,

46
00:03:09,759 --> 00:03:14,020
use the pool math calculator to calculate how much you will need to add or remove from your pool.

47
00:03:14,599 --> 00:03:20,639
Remember, the only way to remove cyanuric acid is by lowering water levels and adding fresh water.

48
00:03:21,219 --> 00:03:23,300
So take special care when adding CYA.

49
00:03:24,719 --> 00:03:27,520
Once your CYA is at proper levels, you can move on to testing free chlorine.

50
00:03:28,340 --> 00:03:32,699
An FAS DPD test kit is required for the slam process which will allow you to read the high chlorine

51
00:03:32,699 --> 00:03:34,180
levels required to shock the pool.

52
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:36,259
If your pool is as green as ours,

53
00:03:36,479 --> 00:03:40,039
it's likely that you will have a reading of 0 parts per million free chlorine in your pool.

54
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:48,759
Next, it's time to determine the shock level you will use to slam your pool by referring to the trouble free pool CYA chlorine chart.

55
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:54,060
This chart lists the free chlorine shock level that corresponds to the CYA reading you took earlier.

56
00:03:54,379 --> 00:03:58,280
The pool we worked on had a CYA reading of 30 parts per million.

57
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:03,439
So according to the chart, we need to reach a shock level of 12 parts per million free chlorine.

58
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:08,819
Use the pool math calculator to determine how much chlorine you will need to reach shock level.

59
00:04:09,159 --> 00:04:10,039
We need it to add to 940 to 1840.

60
00:04:10,039 --> 00:04:10,039
We need it to add to 12% chance.

61
00:04:10,060 --> 00:04:14,539
3 and a half gallons of 10% liquid chlorine to reach 12 parts per million.

62
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:22,319
Make sure you leave your pump running 24-7 while slamming your pool to ensure proper circulation and filtration of the water.

63
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:26,259
Oftentimes many people will shock their pools and call it a day,

64
00:04:26,699 --> 00:04:30,680
but the first part of the slam process is useless without the last, which is maintaining shock level.

65
00:04:31,279 --> 00:04:33,660
Because chlorine is consumed by organic material in sunlight,

66
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,800
the chlorine level will constantly be depleting as algae is killed off.

67
00:04:37,019 --> 00:04:43,240
It's extremely important to maintain your required shock level to ensure that the algae will not bounce back if free chlorine levels drop.

68
00:04:43,879 --> 00:04:49,060
We recommend testing free chlorine every couple hours at the start of the slam process and continue adding the appropriate

69
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:50,879
amount of chlorine to maintain shock level.

70
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:52,600
As algae is killed off,

71
00:04:52,819 --> 00:04:56,319
the chlorine will start to be consumed more slowly and won't need to be checked as often.

72
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:04,040
Now that you have chlorine in your pool and you're maintaining your proper shock level, the waiting game begins.

73
00:05:04,519 --> 00:05:10,060
It's important to backwash or clean your filter daily to remove dead algae that your filtration system is picked up.

74
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:15,779
Continue to vacuum your pool floor each day to get rid of dead algae that has settled to the bottom

75
00:05:15,779 --> 00:05:20,740
and don't forget to brush your pool walls to dislodge algae which is clinging to the sides of your pool.

76
00:05:21,139 --> 00:05:27,800
You should see a noticeable difference each day as your pool transitions from green to cloudy blue to clear.

77
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:31,680
Once the pool is clear, it's time to perform the overnight chlorine loss test.

78
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:35,839
This test will let you know if there's any more algae remaining in the pool.

79
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:40,800
First, take a chlorine test in the evening after the sun has gone down and record the levels.

80
00:05:41,339 --> 00:05:44,259
In the morning before the sun comes up, test your free chlorine again.

81
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:49,279
If the reading has stayed the same or has dropped less than one part per million and your combined chlorine

82
00:05:49,279 --> 00:05:54,300
is less than 0.5, then there are no more organic contaminants in your water and you've passed the OCLT.

83
00:05:54,899 --> 00:05:59,800
However, if your free chlorine has dropped more than one part per million and your combined chlorine is above 0

84
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:05,740
.5, then you will need to continue to maintain your pool at shock level and perform the OCLT the following night.

85
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:08,959
Once the OCLT has passed, you've completed the slam process.

86
00:06:10,399 --> 00:06:12,040
Now that your pool is looking great again,

87
00:06:12,259 --> 00:06:17,199
it's important to maintain your target chlorine level in relation to the CYA levels in the pool.

88
00:06:17,779 --> 00:06:23,480
Perform weekly tests of your pH, free chlorine, and CYA and brush and vacuum your pool weekly.

89
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:29,240
For a more in-depth look at the pool we slammed, visit us over at inyopools.com forward slash blog.

90
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:32,620
If you want to perform the slam process on your pool after watching this video,

91
00:06:33,079 --> 00:06:38,040
feel free to leave a comment down below that includes your test results and pool size and we'll do our best to help you out.

92
00:06:38,740 --> 00:06:38,959
Don't forget to subscribe to our channel and share our channel.

93
00:06:38,980 --> 00:06:41,399
Don't forget to like and subscribe and we'll see you on the next video.

